    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-4642",
      "publishedDate": "2026-11-27T14:15:22.704Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-11-27T14:15:22.704Z",
      "description": "Incorrect Authorization vulnerability in ABB Relion Protection Relays REX610, ABB Relion Protection Relays RE_611 IEC/CN, ABB Relion Protection Relays RBX615, ABB Relion Protection Relays REF615 ANSI, ABB Relion Protection Relays REF615R ANSI, ABB Relion Protection Relays RER615, ABB Relion Protection Relays REC615, ABB Relion Protection Relays REX615, ABB Relion Protection Relays 615 series IEC, ABB Relion Protection Relays 615 series CN, ABB Relion Protection Relays 615 series ANSI, ABB Relion Protection Relays RER620 ANSI, ABB Relion Protection Relays 620 series ANSI, ABB Relion Protection Relays 620 series IEC/CN, and ABB Substation Merging Unit SMU615.\n\nThis issue affects Relion Protection Relays REX610: 1.0, 1.1, and 1.2; Relion Protection Relays RE_611 IEC/CN: 1.0 and 2.0; Relion Protection Relays RBX615: 1.0 and 2.0; Relion Protection Relays REF615 ANSI: 4.1; Relion Protection Relays REF615R ANSI: 4.0 and 4.0 FP1; Relion Protection Relays RER615: 1.0, 1.1, and 2.0; Relion Protection Relays REC615: 1.0, 1.1, and 2.0; Relion Protection Relays REX615: PCL1 (6.0); Relion Protection Relays 615 series IEC: 3.1, 4.0, 4.0 FP1, 5.0, and 5.0 FP1; Relion Protection Relays 615 series CN: 3.1, 4.1, and 5.0 FP1; Relion Protection Relays 615 series ANSI: 4.0, 4.0 FP1, 4.0 FP2, and 5.0 FP1; Relion Protection Relays RER620 ANSI: 1.1, 1.2, and 1.3; Relion Protection Relays 620 series ANSI: 2.0 and 2.0 FP1; Relion Protection Relays 620 series IEC/CN: 2.0 and 2.0 FP1; Substation Merging Unit SMU615: 1.0.",
      "severity": 6.6,
